{"id":"word:hebrew:H339","type":"word","title":"אִי","subtitle":"H339 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, a habitable spot (as desirable); dry land , a coast , an island","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אִי (H339) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 36 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אִי (ʼîy) means properly, a habitable spot (as desirable); dry land , a coast , an island First listed occurrence: Dan 11 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אִי","transliteration":"ʼîy","pronunciation":"ee","strong":"H339","lemmaId":"hebrew:H339","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אִיִּ֖ים","אִיִּ֥ים","אִיֵּ֤י","אִיִּים֙","אִיִּ֣ים"],"morphs":[["HNcmpa",11],["HTd/Ncmpa",6],["HRd/Ncmpa",4],["HR/Ncmpc",3],["HNcmpc",3],["HTj",3],["HTd/Ncmsa",2],["HR/Ncmpa",1],["HC/Ncmpc",1],["HC/R/Ncmpc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, a habitable spot (as desirable); dry land , a coast , an island","usage":"country, isle, island.","full":"H339. i I. אִי noun masculine Isa 20:5 ( feminine 23:2 ) coast, region 339 (contracted from אֱוִי so Ol § 152 b ; place whither one betakes oneself for resting, etc., originally from mariner's standpoint) — אִי absolute 20:6 +; construct Jer 47:4 ; ( Job 22:30 see below IV. אִי compare Di) plural אִיִּים Psa 72:10 +; אִיִּן Ezek 26:18 (Co איים ) אִיֵּי Gen 10:5 +; — coast, border, region (mostly late), of Philistia & Phenicia with adjacent country Isa 20:6 ; 23:2 , 6 ; so of Caphtor (= Crete) Jer 47:4 ; הַיָּם בְּעֵבֶר אֲשֶׁר הָאִי מַלְכֵי 25:22 ; elswhere plural, coasts of Chittim 2:10 ; Ezek 27:6 , of Elishah 27:7 ; different countries (on or in sea) 27:3 ; 27:15 ; 27:35 ; 26:15 , 18 (twice in verse) (last strike out Co compare ᵐ5 ) compare 39:6 , so also הַגּוֺיִם אִיֵּי Gen 10:5 (P); particular הַיָּם אִיֵּי = coast-lands & islands Isa 11:11 ; 24:15 , || הָאָרֶץ Est 10:1 ; see (without הַיָּם ) Dan 11:18 , & Psa 72:10 ; so often Isa 2 including inhabitants, 41:1 , 5 ; 42:4 , 10 ( וְישְׁבֵיהֶם אִיִּים || וּמְלֹאוֺ הַיָּם ) Isa 42:12 ; 49:1 ; 51:5 ; 59:18 ; 60:9 ; 66:19 ; compare Jer 31:10 ; Psa 97:1 ; Zeph 2:11 ( הַגּוֺיִם אִיֵּי ); islands , distinctly (taken up by ׳א as little things) Isa 40:15 ; coasts, banks , i.e. habitable lands 42:15 (|| נְהָרוֺת ). I. אִי noun masculine isle, coast , see I. אָוָה .","rootNote":"from 183 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Dan 11 18","keyReferences":["Dan 11 18","Esth 10 1","Ezek 26 15","Ezek 26 18","Ezek 26 18","Ezek 27 3","Ezek 27 6","Ezek 27 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":36,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Dan 11 18","book":"Dan","chapter":11,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/אִיִּ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"Esth 10 1","book":"Esth","chapter":10,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אִיֵּ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmpc"},{"reference":"Ezek 26 15","book":"Ezek","chapter":26,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אִיִּֽים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"Ezek 26 18","book":"Ezek","chapter":26,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָֽ/אִיִּ֔ן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"Ezek 26 18","book":"Ezek","chapter":26,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אִיִּ֥ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmpa"},{"reference":"Ezek 27 3","book":"Ezek","chapter":27,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אִיִּ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmpa"},{"reference":"Ezek 27 6","book":"Ezek","chapter":27,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵ/אִיֵּ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmpc"},{"reference":"Ezek 27 7","book":"Ezek","chapter":27,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מֵ/אִיֵּ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncmpc"},{"reference":"Ezek 27 15","book":"Ezek","chapter":27,"verse":15,"englishTex